From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=A1nos=20Mik=C3=B3?=
 <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 15:22:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 021/154] atrium: open links in Atrium's own split from the
 link context menu
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

'Open Link in Split View' was hidden on Atrium windows because stock
TabStripModel::AddToNewSplit NOTREACHED-crashes for them: Atrium's split is an
AtriumPaneContainerView hosting two WebContents in one window and never touches
TabCollection, so the index AddToNewSplit resolves does not exist in its tree.

Re-route rather than repair. Making TabStripModel compatible with split_tabs
bookkeeping Atrium deliberately does not use would be large and buy nothing,
since Atrium's own split already works end to end.

The earlier crash guard is relocated, not weakened: the item becomes visible
again, and the gate moves to OpenLinkInSplitView - the single choke point both
the menu item and the layout submenu dispatch through - so AddToNewSplit stays
reachable only when Atrium is disabled. Non-Atrium windows are unchanged.

Exposed through atrium_feature_check.h, the established pattern for a narrow
Atrium call reachable from cross-platform code. No new host op, no Swift hop.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../render_view_context_menu.cc               | 36 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc b/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
index 5e4a460ef85c8..2f355d5cfa6f2 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
@@ -1920,17 +1920,15 @@ void RenderViewContextMenu::AppendLinkItems() {
       // Opening a link in split view should also go through the same
       // constraints as opening a link in a new tab since a split view tab is a
       // new tab that is then joined with the current active tab.
-      // Atrium windows have no BrowserView-backed TabCollection (crash-guard
-      // posture: split view is architecturally incompatible with Atrium's
-      // single-tab-per-window sidebar model) - AddToNewSplit NOTREACHEDs at
-      // components/tabs/impl/tab_collection.cc:221 if this item is invoked
-      // on an Atrium window (found via routing Task 7's VM probing).
-      // Suppress the item outright rather than patch stock split-tab code.
-      // atrium::IsAtriumBrowserWindowEnabled() is per-process (connected()),
-      // not per-window, but a connected dylib implies every window is an
-      // Atrium window, so the check is equivalent here (mirrors
-      // tab_helpers.cc's identical SadTabHelper gate).
-      if (IsNormalBrowser() && !atrium::IsAtriumBrowserWindowEnabled()) {
+      // Atrium windows have no BrowserView-backed TabCollection, so
+      // stock's AddToNewSplit NOTREACHEDs at
+      // components/tabs/impl/tab_collection.cc:221 if invoked on one (found
+      // via routing Task 7's VM probing). Rather than suppress the item, the
+      // EXECUTION side (OpenLinkInSplitView below) re-routes into Atrium's
+      // own split when atrium::IsAtriumBrowserWindowEnabled() - the stock
+      // AddToNewSplit call stays reachable only when that gate is false, so
+      // this visibility check no longer needs to know about Atrium at all.
+      if (IsNormalBrowser()) {
         tabs::TabInterface* tab =
             tabs::TabInterface::MaybeGetFromContents(GetWebContents());
         auto [string_id, icon] = GetOpenLinkInSplitStringAndIcon(
@@ -5695,6 +5693,22 @@ void RenderViewContextMenu::OpenLinkInSplitView(
   CHECK(browser);
   CHECK(browser->GetType() == BrowserWindowInterface::TYPE_NORMAL);
 
+  // Atrium's split is AtriumPaneContainerView, not stock
+  // split_tabs/TabCollection - the AddToNewSplit call below NOTREACHEDs for
+  // an Atrium window (see atrium_feature_check.h's doc on
+  // OpenLinkInAtriumSplit). Re-route there instead; AddToNewSplit stays
+  // reachable below only when the gate is false.
+  if (atrium::IsAtriumBrowserWindowEnabled()) {
+    OpenURLParams url_params = GetOpenURLParamsWithExtraHeaders(
+        params_.link_url, params_.frame_url, params_.frame_origin,
+        WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_BACKGROUND_TAB, ui::PAGE_TRANSITION_LINK,
+        /*extra_headers=*/std::string(), /*started_from_context_menu=*/true);
+    atrium::OpenLinkInAtriumSplit(
+        browser, source_web_contents_, url_params,
+        layout == split_tabs::SplitTabLayout::kStacked);
+    return;
+  }
+
   TabStripModel* const tab_strip_model = browser->GetTabStripModel();
   tabs::TabInterface* const source_tab =
       tabs::TabInterface::MaybeGetFromContents(source_web_contents_);
